Answer: The variable is static, so it can be accessed with the interface name, and it can also be accessed with the name of the implementing class.

```java
interface Calculator {
int x = 10;
}
class Demo implements Calculator { }
public class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
System.out.println(Calculator.x);
System.out.println(Demo.x);
}
}
```

Output: 10 10 Explanation: both expressions read the same public static final variable.

